WEBVTT

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:00.810
"Class 1"

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:02.180
An errand?

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:07.230
Yes. We're all going to be doing
a play for the school festival.

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.570
We can do whatever play we want.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:13.280
So Filo, I want you to pick
the theme for the play.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:14.700
The theme?

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.740
Yes, why don't you go talk to a bunch of people

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:22.160
about what kind of play they want,
and then come up with an idea.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.290
I think you need that experience.

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:26.290
Can you do it?

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.330
Okay!

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:28.960
I'll do my best!

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.010
I'm counting on you, Filo!

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:31.960
Okay!

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:02.680
"Episode 9: Investigate! First Errand"

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.680
Huh? There's a school festival?

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.390
That's what they said.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:10.060
Mr. Ros-<i>chi</i> never tells us the important stuff.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:12.940
And all the classes are doing a play?

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:16.110
Yup. What kind of story do you like?

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.240
What kind of story...

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.990
I want to see a story about my lord!

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:23.910
Doing a play about an undead
in front of a goddess!

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.490
Not a chance!

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:27.330
And stop nodding.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:29.040
--Death Knight disappeared!
--Again?

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.040
--Death Knight disappeared!
--Aqua!

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.000
If you want to call yourself a goddess, fine,
but try to get along with others!

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.720
I'm not just calling myself a goddess!
I am a goddess!

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:40.930
Well, I think you should be nicer,

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:44.890
but Lord Ains told me to
"be nice to the <i>tsundere</i>."

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.020
What does that mean?

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.560
It means you're a <i>tsundere</i>.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:52.270
You're mean to the person you like.

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:56.070
Aqua, the minute you got lectured
by a kid, you already lost.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:03:00.360
--Why?
--Oh, Death Knight's back.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.990
Why not talk to more people?

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:07.290
Yeah, I will! Thanks!

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.250
It's the skeleton man...
grandpa... skeleton guy!

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.460
She tried really hard there.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:17.340
I'm Ains.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.460
What is it?

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.260
Do you need to talk to me?

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:25.260
Um, I'm talking to a lot of people right now!

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.430
A play, huh?

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:29.390
Yes.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:32.520
Hamsuke said he wanted to see
the story of an undead...

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.810
That's wonderful!

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:37.940
A story to tell everyone
how wonderful Lord Ains is!

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:41.740
Truly a worthy gift to a supreme being!

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:43.030
Indeed!

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.280
And I can be his empress...

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:48.160
Did you say something, lamprey?

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.910
Did you say something, big-mouthed gorilla?

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.410
Calm down, both of you.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:54.830
--Okay!
--Perfect harmony!

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:00.760
Filo, I'm sorry, but we don't
know much about drama.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.050
You'd do better to ask someone else.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:05.300
For example?

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:09.680
Hmm... How about Kazuma's gang?

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:12.100
Explosion!

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.060
Well?

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:18.480
Hmm...

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.110
The firepower is concentrated on
a single point, and extremely effective.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:25.200
Collateral damage is minimal.
An excellent explosion.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.910
What score would you give it?

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.120
Forty points.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:31.700
If you can't shorten the incantation,
it will be difficult to use in combat.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:34.080
A short incantation is out of the question.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.170
They aren't cool!

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:40.750
What's important is casting time. Not coolness.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:41.920
Not true.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:45.260
No, on the battlefield, a single second
means the difference between life and death.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.140
Shorten the incantation time

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.600
--Hey, Tanya.
--to efficiently...

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.930
Her incantations are a mystery.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:57.350
We don't even know if she needs
an incantation to cast a spell at all.

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:59.190
She says something different every time.

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:02.440
If I don't use a cool incantation, I will die.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:05.280
Are you making fun of me?

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:07.200
Are you making fun of me?

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.950
Is it good, Filo?

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:11.040
It's good!

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.710
This is tough.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.920
Everybody says something different.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.630
Hey there.

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:20.460
The girl from Class 2!

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.090
You seemed like something
was really bothering you.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.210
Is something wrong?

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:27.720
Um, I'm searching for a theme.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:28.800
A theme?

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:34.350
Yes. We're doing something called
a "play" at the school festival.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:36.560
A play at the school festival?

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:41.440
I was asked to find a theme.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:44.490
So you're going around
to talk to everybody, huh?

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:48.280
But everybody says
something different, so it's hard.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.820
Why not go to the library then?

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:52.910
There's a lot of books there,

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:56.210
so I'm sure you'll find what you're looking for.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:57.830
The library?

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.790
Got it! Thanks, miss!

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:03.460
She's a good girl.

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:05.010
Yup.

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:07.220
Anyway, we have to go find Roswaal and say,

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:10.760
"We didn't hear anything
about a school festival."

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:11.760
Yup.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.720
But, Puck,

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:17.020
here he's "Mr. Roswaal."

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.560
Okay.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:18.850
"Library"

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:23.270
That book's easy to read. I think
it'll give you some good ideas, too.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:25.400
"Gentle Fairy Tales"

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.400
Now take it and go.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:31.740
Okay, I'll have Master read it to me.

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.780
Thank you, Mare!

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:35.040
Beat...

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:35.950
Beako!

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:37.580
It's not Beako, I wonder!

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:39.670
Bye!

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:42.750
What a rude girl!

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:49.470
Can I ask something?

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:51.010
Yes.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.590
What is it?

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:54.720
Nothing important.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:58.640
Do you remember how you got to the school?

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:02.730
Lord Ains said he pushed a button.

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:07.530
Lord Ains apologized and said it was his fault.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:12.030
But he's a supreme being,
so he must have had some reason.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:12.870
I see.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:16.830
It's nice to have the person
you believe in right next to you.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:19.620
Do you not, Beatrice?

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.540
Not anymore, I wonder.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.420
What about Subaru?

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:28.260
I can't trust that guy at all!

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:30.130
Oh, yeah.

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:31.550
Yeah, I wonder.

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:36.100
What've you got there?

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:38.430
Oh, the wolf girl!

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:41.190
Yup. The wolf girl!

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:44.980
And the girl who's very interested
in what you've got there!

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:45.020
"Gentle Fairy Tales"

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:51.820
This? I got it to help pick the theme
for the school festival.

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:53.200
What about this?

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:56.910
A poor little bird is tricked by an evil man
and turned into fried chicken--

00:07:56.910 --> 00:08:00.200
Don't make up stories!

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:02.290
The girls with black hair!

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:07.630
You were told by Lord Ains
to follow the rules of the school.

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:13.090
I'm just trying to see how far
I can bend the rules, is all.

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:15.800
Your name's Filo, right?

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:18.760
You're looking for a theme for Class 1's play?

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:24.520
Yes. And Mare and Beako gave me a book to help!

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:25.690
Mare gave it to you?

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:28.570
Very well. We'll think of something with you.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:32.190
How about a story where a poor raccoon
is tricked by a man with--

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:34.490
You just did that.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:37.240
But a normal story is boring!

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.200
We're the ones who'll be the acting!

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.080
It's boring!

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:41.410
And Narberal's a terrible actor--

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:45.000
--A terrible what now?
--Oww! Oww!

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.960
But if we're going to act, it would
be better if we could be ourselves.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:52.630
Though Narberal wouldn't be able
to talk about anything but murder!

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:55.130
--What did you say?
--Oww!

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:57.590
What are you ladies talking about?

00:08:57.590 --> 00:09:00.470
None of your business,
you piece of human garbage.

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:02.770
--Scary words from such a pretty lady.
--Yup.

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:07.230
Hearing that from you ugly insects
means nothing to me.

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:09.730
That's it!

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:11.690
The ugly duckling!

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:15.200
The ugly duckling gets terribly insulted
by the other ducklings!

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:18.490
You could just be who you already are!

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:20.450
Yes, that could work in some cases...

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.790
It's perfect for you, since you're so violent.

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:25.830
--Who are you calling violent?
--Oww! Oww! Oww!

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:27.960
<i>The Ugly Duckling</i>?

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:31.090
Got it! Thanks, ladies!

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:32.630
And old guys, too!

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:33.880
Yeah, you're wel--

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:35.340
We're not old!

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:35.470
"And they lived happily ever after."

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:36.880
"Class 1"

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:39.430
"The End."

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:40.430
Well, Filo?

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:42.810
Yes, I like it!

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:45.270
Naofumi, this is wonderful!

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:46.270
Let's go with this!

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:48.060
You like it that much?

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:49.360
Yes, I do!

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.570
Yeah, it's a great story.

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:55.610
"The real me was actually very noble."

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:57.780
Why are you looking at me when you say that?

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:00.160
Is it okay, Felt?

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.200
Um...

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:07.370
Okay, Class 1 will do <i>The Ugly Duckling</i>!

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:08.870
Okay!

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:12.040
Master, I worked really hard!

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:14.420
Yes, well done.

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:17.470
Naofumi, if you'd just asked me...

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:18.430
Sorry.

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:20.510
Next time, I'll have you do something.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:22.640
Don't treat me like a child!

00:10:22.640 --> 00:11:50.787
Jeez...
